.TH CAPTWIRE 1 "August 2026" "capt6000 1.0" "capt6000"
.SH NAME
captwire \- decode a raw CAPT wire capture into readable commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B captwire
.RB [ \-v ]
.I capture
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B captwire
reads a raw CAPT byte stream \(em such as the one the backend writes when
.B CAPT_SINK
points at a file \(em and prints each protocol packet as a command name
with its payload length, decoding the sub\-commands of
.B SET_PARMS
and hex\-dumping short payloads.  A summary of the page data volume is
printed at the end.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: also list every
.B PRINT_DATA
packet instead of only counting them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 if no capture file was given, and 1 on a read
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR captdump (1),
.BR captstat (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Viktor Hozhyi.  Part of capt6000,
.UR https://github.com/ViktorGozhiy/capt6000
.UE .
